# Survival Analysis Actuarial Project

This project applies survival analysis techniques to time-to-event data, with a focus on actuarial and insurance-related risk modelling.

## Project Objectives

The main objectives of this project are to:

- Estimate survival probabilities using the Kaplan-Meier estimator
- Compare survival experiences across different groups
- Apply the Cox proportional hazards model to identify key risk factors
- Interpret statistical results in an actuarial and insurance context

## Tools Used

- R
- survival package
- survminer package
- Excel

## Methods

### Kaplan-Meier Estimation

Kaplan-Meier estimation is used to estimate the survival function and visualise survival probabilities over time.

### Cox Proportional Hazards Model

The Cox proportional hazards model is used to examine how explanatory variables affect the hazard rate.

## Expected Output

The project will generate:

- Survival curves
- Cox model results
- Interpretation of key risk factors
- Business insights for insurance and actuarial decision-making

